  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\int -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{7}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}ln\u2061|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
